1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
[gasps]

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
[Knuckle] No way.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Where could he have gone
in that condition?

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

5
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
[singer singing in English]

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
[singer singing in English]

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,000
[singer singing in English]

9
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

10
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
[Shaiapouf] Will he do it,

11
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
abandon his original intent

12
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
and commit to an answer
without evidence?

13
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
[grunts]

14
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
[Shaiapouf chuckles]

15
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
He won't.

16
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
[Shaiapouf] I see
you've made your choice.

17
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
[Morel] Once I thought about it,
it was simple.

18
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Your pupa appeared
after I played my card.

19
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Since you only hid
after learning my agenda,

20
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
I knew that was your ability
and that it was a trap.

21
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
And the fact
that you didn't respond

22
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
when I lifted up my pipe
to strike you confirmed it.

23
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
In fact, you showed no signs
of reacting at all.

24
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Didn't make any sense.

25
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
[Shaiapouf laughs]

26
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
[Morel gasps]

27
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Fifteen minutes.

28
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
[chuckles]

29
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
That was how long
I expected you to take

30
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
I fully intended
to slip through the smoke

31
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,000
and move about the area freely.

32
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
I decided to take advantage
of that misconception

33
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
and quietly dispose of your friends.

34
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
So you thought I'd wait that long
in front of an empty husk?

35
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Well, if that's how
he slipped through Smoky Jail,

36
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
I would never have
been able to see a thing.

37
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
[gasps]

38
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
[Shaiapouf] You should
have waited longer,

39
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
because my strategy to slip through
was a last resort.

40
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
But if I'm being perfectly honest,

41
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
I was quite upset about being trapped.

42
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,000
That's a crap diversion, and you're lying!

43
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
You made it through the smoke just fine.

44
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
[Shaiapouf] Well, true.

45
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
At that point,
that was all there was to it.

46
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
-[laughter continues]
-I was convinced

47
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:15,000
But you made some wild guesses
and removed the barrier.

48
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

49
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

50
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Smoke Troopers, Deep Purple!

51
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
[laughing]

52
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
[Morel] I can't destroy them?

53
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
They just divide and reassemble.

54
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Are they invincible?

55
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
[laughing continues]

56
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
[together] Thank you! Bye-bye!

57
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[Morel] Don't be fooled.

58
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
He's playing mind games.

59
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
My decision to attack
was the best option at the time.

60
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:16,000
No, I'm already playing into his hands
by dwelling on the past.

61
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:21,000
If I'm gonna win this,
I've got to anticipate his next moves.

62
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
To join up with the rest
of the Royal Guard,

63
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,000
to find and eliminate my companions,

64
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
and to reunite with the King.
That must be it.

65
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
His goals are the same as mine.

66
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
No problem.

67
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Huh?

68
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
[dramatic music playing]

69
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,000
[groans]

70
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
[laughs]

71
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
[Morel] He got me.

72
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,000
I can't use any other moves.

73
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
If I deactivate Deep Purple,
I'll be defenseless.

74
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] Hey, are you the one…

75
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
who can teleport?

76
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,000
[gasps]

77
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[guitar music playing]

78
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Hmm?

79
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,000
What in the hell
did you do with Shoot, huh?

80
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
What's that?

81
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Hmm?

82
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
[Morel] Eighty-nine Deep Purple puppets,

83
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
the most I can produce right now.

84
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,000
I'll use them to help Knuckle
as best I can.

85
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
I'll take your life!

86
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
[door creaks]

87
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
Okay. There's no one here.

88
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Good. Time to escape, so let's go.

89
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Damn it. They told us
we were gonna be safe here.

90
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
It's too bad
I can't get in touch with Sir Leol.

91
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Oh, I know!

92
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
I can make you my deputy.
How's that sound?

93
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
[man] Help me.

94
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Huh?

95
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Please help me.

96
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Get me out of here!

97
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
I need help.

98
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
You don't look so good, Director Bizeff.

99
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
No, I… can't move my legs.

100
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Hmm?

101
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Hmm.

102
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
If you do, I'm gonna die!

103
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Yeah, no can do.

104
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
There's no way I can move all that stuff.

105
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
At the very least, call someone to help!

106
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,000
I told you no already!

107
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,000
I'm trying to get out of here A.S.A.P.

108
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,000
My boss is missing,
I have no direct line to the King,

109
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Just tell me what you want!

110
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:34,000
There are mountains of treasure
in the basement!

111
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,000
so please, please pull me out!

112
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
[Hina] Where in the basement?

113
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:46,000
[Bizeff] There's a private area
reserved for the leader

114
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
that's located just beyond the shelter.

115
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I'm in charge of the vault.

116
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
I'm the only one who has access.
[groaning]

117
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
You'll give me anything?

118
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Oh, my.

119
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
You'd better keep your promise,

120
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
or I'm gonna kill you, okay?

121
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[singing] ♪ Treasure, treasure ♪

122
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
♪ We're off
To find some treasure ♪

123
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
♪ Some pretty golden treasure… ♪

124
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[Bizeff] This country
is absolutely done for.

125
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
I wasn't certain before,

126
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,000
but an air raid without my consultation

127
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
is all the proof I need.

128
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
I'm sure they're calling
the Ants' biological weapons

129
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
to justify the assault.

130
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
If I'm captured,
they'll force me to confess

131
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
and use it as cover
while they throw me in prison for life.

132
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:47,000
That, or they'll execute me
so I can't talk.

133
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
[groans]

134
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
[Shaiapouf] Now the smoke user's
out of commission.

135
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,000
the King will only find me a nuisance.

136
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Beelzebub!

137
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
the smallest being nano-sized particles.

138
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:44,000
He can divide himself
into a variety of sizes,

139
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
and the smaller they are,

140
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
the greater in number they can be.

141
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
However, no matter
the size of his clones,

142
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
[Shaiapouf] Oh, smoke man,

143
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
if you hadn't removed the barrier,

144
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
my main body would never
have been able to escape,

145
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:08,000
and my combat capacity
would have been reduced by half.

146
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:13,000
I'm sure a puppet master
such as yourself is acutely aware

147
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
of the incomparable
difference in strength

148
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
between a clone and your own body.

149
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
You've already lost.

150
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
You should have deliberated
a little more carefully.

151
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
When you realized
the pupa was empty,

152
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
you could have asked yourself

153
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:36,000
whether its contents
had escaped the smoke

154
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
or whether they remained inside.

155
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
for quite a long time,

156
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
and some might have been fooled,

157
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,000
but as long as a few
were as skilled as you seem to be,

158
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
they would have realized
that I was a fake,

159
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
sooner or later, anyway.

160
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
and would have searched for me.

161
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
And in that case,

162
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
I would have had no way to fight you,

163
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:34,000
given my reduced state of being.

164
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,000
[squish]

165
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
In other words,

166
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,000
if you'd kept me imprisoned
as per your initial plan,

167
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
you might have lost
some colleagues,

168
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
but you would have
been able to defeat me.

169
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Truth be told, I was 10% resigned
to that outcome.

170
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Your emotions were perfectly aligned
to accomplish that.

171
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[sighs] Such a pity.

172
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
He then faced Pouf in a battle of wits

173
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:51,000
and it was certainly more than
a simple product of coincidence.

174
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,000
It would be safe to say Morel's
vast wealth of experience

175
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
played a role in saving him.

176
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Not long after entering the palace,

177
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Morel immediately began to prepare

178
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:06,000
by weighing the strength of the enemies
against that of his own team.

179
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Deep down, he knew
they had underestimated

180
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
the power of those
they would be fighting.

181
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] The real one's
hidden among the fakes,

182
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
trying to attack me, right?

183
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
This time, I'm gonna land
a counterpunch on him.

184
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
[Morel] Seventy-five left. Seventy-two…

185
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
down to seventy.

186
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
[dramatic music playing]

187
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,000
and there's a boy close by
who's likely an enemy.

188
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Three more are near
the underground shelter,

189
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Hina, a Soldier Ant, and Bizeff!

190
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,000
They may be heading underground.

191
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Welfin is behind them.

192
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
He appears to be in pursuit.

193
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
I see.

194
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
The girl was injured by a dragon arrow.

195
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Why doesn't the enemy
take this chance to attack Pitou?

196
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Could he know the girl?

197
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
East tower antechamber.

198
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
[gasps] This area is
simply crawling with enemies.

199
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
One, two, three…

200
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
[gasps] But Youpi is taking
them out quickly.

201
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
It's the smoke guy and a bunch of thugs.

202
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:34,000
And there's a weird
pointy-headed fat thing.

203
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Not sure if it's friend or foe.

204
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
It should take Youpi less than
a minute to find the real one.

205
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
[gasps]

206
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
The King is gone.

207
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:18,000
[Menthuthuyoupi chuckles] What's wrong?
You're running out of clones.

208
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Is that it?

209
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Should I give him an opening?

210
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
If I do, it'll make it easier
for him to hit me.

211
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Be careful now.

212
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Make it look natural.

213
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Here you go.

214
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Come on!

215
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
You bastard.

216
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,000
[Morel] Do you finally get it, sucker?

217
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:15,000
See, there never was
a real one in the first place.

218
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] I'll kill you!

219
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
[intense music playing]

220
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Yeah, no kidding, dumbass!

221
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:44,000
[Shaiapouf] An aura explosion from Youpi?

222
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Did he really need to use
such an ability?

223
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:01,000
But even so, locating the King
is my top priority.

224
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
[Knuckle] Thanks, boss.

225
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
If you hadn't set that condition,

226
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
I would have snapped and charged him.

227
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
It's a good thing you did.

228
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,000
[Morel] Listen up.
The only time I'll make

229
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
those pissed-lookin' clones of you

230
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
is when you've flown off the handle

231
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,000
and stopped paying attention to anything.

232
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:25,000
When you see 'em, blend in
with the clones best you can.

233
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Just take a breather,
and refocus on your goal.

234
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Yeah, I get it.

235
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
That's enough with the lecture.

236
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
After cooling down
and thinking about it,

237
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:40,000
there's no way that Youpi
would have taken Shoot.

238
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:44,000
But if Shoot couldn't move around
on his own, then who did?

239
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
[growls] Stop overthinking.

240
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:51,000
I need to focus
on the opponent in front of me!

241
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,000
That was…

242
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,000
-[Bizeff groans]
-[Hina wails]

243
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Hey, hurry up, and get in
before the entrance is blocked up!

244
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
[Welfin] Damn it! Bizeff is mine.

245
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:35,000
If I knew what abilities they had,
I could make a move.

246
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[gasps]

247
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,000
[scoffs]

248
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
